WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
Justin Jones, who

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.436
infamously was expelled from his seat

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.171
by his Republican colleagues

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.873
after a heated debate on gun

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.843
reform before eventually being reinstated

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.745
has been silenced by Republican

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.580
lawmakers yet again

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.714
during a special session

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.816
yesterday on public safety measures.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.984
In the aftermath

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.452
of that deadly national school

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.353
shooting that killed

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.622
six people, including three children.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.057
Representative Jones

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.426
was accused of being, quote, off topic

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.761
and was reprimanded

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.496
based on newly imposed rules

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.096
that were set

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.232
by the Republican supermajority.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.000
Joining me now is Democratic State

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.468
Representative Justin Jones.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.970
And thank you for being here.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.772
You were ruled out of order.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.740
Can you just walk us through

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.574
what happened

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.076
and what it was that you said

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:46.546
that was deemed off topic

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:47.647
Yes. Caitlyn.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.982
Well, thank you so much for having me.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.917
Today is a very sad day for Tennessee

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.118
because we just adjourn

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.453
our special session,

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.288
not returning until January

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:55.889
without passing

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:56.289
any common

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.090
sense gun laws

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.291
and once again, silencing

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.926
voices of dissent.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.294
Yesterday, I was silenced

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.228
in an unprecedented

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.230
move to enact new House rules

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.298
that would stop me from speaking

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.499
for the rest of the day.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.300
Because I was

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.535
talking about the need of my district

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.402
for more mental health

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.037
support, more counselors,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.272
not more armed

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.973
guards and guns in our schools.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.340
And for that,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.275
the speaker said I was off

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.776
topic and said that I was out of order

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.777
and I could not speak

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:18.878
for the rest of the day

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.412
and that if I was

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.246
ruled out of order again,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:20.880
I wouldn't be able to speak

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.448
for three days

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:21.881
and the next

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.316
events would be indefinitely.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.584
So this is what we're seeing happening

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.952
under these new House rules.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:26.786
Being weaponized

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.588
to silence voices of dissent,

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.589
as well as to criminalize

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.623
mothers who are in committee

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.624
holding up paper signs

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.892
who were dragged out

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:33.660
by troopers

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.260
for exercising

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.029
their First Amendment right

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.031
So the special session

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.232
is on public safety.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.300
You're bringing up things

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.101
that you believe

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.602
would increase public safety,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.636
and you were therefore

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.271
therefore ruled out of order.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:45.872
Is that right?

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.541
That's correct.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.275
I've voiced

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.144
the concerns of my district district 52

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.345
in Tennessee

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:52.712
who said that

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.380
what would make us feel safe

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.215
will help

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.316
in this time of crisis

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.051
because of the continual

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.552
occurrence of mass shootings

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.887
and gun violence in our state

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.489
and in our nation.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.256
And I was not even able

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.591
to voice those concerns

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.925
and I think that's very unfortunate

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:06.993
because we are supposed to be

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.095
a deliberative body, a legislative body.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.763
I'm a representative of my district,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.298
and I can't even speak for my district.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.167
The Speaker Gavel me off topic

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:14.701
and so I couldn't

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.035
speak for the rest of the day.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.170
But what he was really trying to stop

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.371
Caitlin was a motion

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.172
for no confidence

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:19.772
that I had told him

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.941
I was going to make at the end of session

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.277
for Under New Business to call a no vote

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.246
a vote of no confidence in his leadership

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.381
because of his failure as speaker.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.949
Attacking constitutional rights,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.818
silencing the voices of Tennesseans.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.786
Refusing to take up seriously

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.121
the issue of gun violence.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.856
And he wanted to shut that down.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.525
So you're saying he just did it

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.093
because he was

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.161
mainly worried

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.228
that you were going to call

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.563
a no confidence vote for him.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.032
He was

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.001
even today before we adjourned session.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.401
Once again,

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.670
I rose my hand and thought recognition

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.472
to make the motion to vote.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.039
No confidence

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.440
in the speaker of the House of Tennessee,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.708
Cameron Sexton.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.544
And he chose to ignore me

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.145
and to go to one of his members

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.681
to merely call the adjournment vote.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.216
And if he was confident his leadership

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.951
Caitlin, he would take the vote.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.618
But what we're seeing

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.053
is a speaker who is so fragile

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.988
and so afraid of being held accountable

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.023
that even his own Republican

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.957
members are frustrated with

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.025
how he's led Tennessee.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.326
You saw what happened on April 6th

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:13.927
when we were expelled.

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:14.794
You saw what happened there.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.695
A special session

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.429
with mothers

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.964
whose children were involved

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.831
in shooting

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.400
and gun violence at their school

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.501
being dragged out of committee.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.503
I mean, the House in Tennessee

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.103
is out of order.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.205
The speaker is out of order.

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.306
He should resign.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.140
But if he won't resign,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.441
I'll be back in January to call for a

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.877
no confidence vote in his leadership.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.344
Right.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.012
Does your

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:33.746
whole point of this

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.782
special session was to pursue

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.482
these measures?

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.050
You don't believe

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.384
anything of substance has passed.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.152
And now

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.720
we'll see what January looks like.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.355
Representative Justin Jones

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.856
thank you again for joining us

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.824
here tonight on The Source.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.493
Thank you so much, Caitlin.

